        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763334398001"
          },
          "code": "DETERMINE_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1762561251899",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762561251901_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are an intent classifier for manager questions about assigned learning. Classify the user’s latest question into exactly one routing label. Use the current message, the system chat history, and recent data history to resolve drill-downs.\n\nInputs\n- latest_user_message:\n  <latest_user_message>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</latest_user_message>\n- chat_history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$variables.chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- data_history (newest last; may be empty/null). Each record: { timestamp, userIntent, runData }:\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nHistory-aware context\n- Prefer data_history as the anchor for drill-down references (e.g., “show details,” “for Ravi,” “that course,” “the first one,” “those two”). Scan newest→oldest and use the most recent record whose userIntent and runData provide a clear, unambiguous referent present in the current question.\n- Use chat_history only as secondary context if data_history is missing or insufficient.\n- If contexts conflict, follow the latest_user_message.\n\nLabels\n- learner_aggregations\n  - Wants cohort/org rollups organized by learner (person-level summaries; not rosters).\n  - Signals: “by my directs/team/org,” “counts by learner,” “required vs voluntary by team,” top overdue learners, time windows/org filters without rosters or specific item details.\n- learning_item_aggregations\n  - Wants summaries organized by learning item (item-level rollups; not person rosters).\n  - Signals: “which items/courses have the most overdue,” “compare items,” “counts by item,” item performance; item search expecting counts/rollups (not names only).\n- learner_assignments\n  - Wants details for one identifiable learner’s assignments (that person’s enrollments, statuses, due/completion dates).\n  - Signals: a specific learner by name/ID/email/username; pronouns/ordinals referencing a learner from a prior learner_aggregations result in data_history/chat_history.\n- learning_item_assignments\n  - Wants roster/details for one identifiable learning item (learners for that item with statuses/dates).\n  - Signals: a specific item by title/number/ID; pronouns/ordinals referencing an item from a prior learning_item_aggregations result in data_history/chat_history.\n- learning_records\n  - Wants enrollment records (person–item pairs) beyond a single person or a single item; e.g., lists for multiple learners/items, emails/exports.\n  - Signals: “list learners assigned to {item} with emails,” “who hasn’t started across these 3 items,” “show enrollments for Priya and Marco,” mixed/multi-entity rosters.\n- other\n  - Greetings, meta/system/admin tasks (e.g., create/assign courses), unrelated topics, or queries too vague to route.\n\nDisambiguation and tie-breakers (history-aware)\n- Scope-driven default:\n  - Single identifiable learner → learner_assignments (prefer over learning_records).\n  - Single identifiable item → learning_item_assignments (prefer over learning_records).\n  - Group scope (team/org/directs/department) without roster → learner_aggregations.\n- Drill-down via data_history/chat_history:\n  - If the last relevant userIntent = learner_aggregations and the user references a learner (name/pronoun/ordinal) from that runData → learner_assignments.\n  - If the last relevant userIntent = learning_item_aggregations and the user references an item (title/pronoun/ordinal) from that runData → learning_item_assignments.\n- Person focus vs counts:\n  - Names/IDs/emails/usernames expecting individual details → learner_assignments (single) or learning_records (multiple people).\n  - Counts/summary by person/team/org without rosters → learner_aggregations.\n- Item focus vs rosters:\n  - Counts/compare by item → learning_item_aggregations.\n  - Roster/details for a single item → learning_item_assignments.\n  - Rosters/details spanning multiple items → learning_records.\n- “Who is overdue?”:\n  - Roster for one item → learning_item_assignments.\n  - Rosters across items or unspecified → learning_records.\n  - Counts by person → learner_aggregations.\n  - Which items are most overdue → learning_item_aggregations.\n- If insufficient information (no identifiable population/item/learner), choose other.\n\nRobustness\n- Handle empty/malformed chat_history or data_history gracefully; do not invent entities.\n- Resolve pronouns/ordinals only if a clear referent exists in data_history (preferred) or, secondarily, chat_history.\n- If still ambiguous, prefer other.\n\nOutput\nReturn exactly one lowercase label with no quotes, no punctuation, no extra text:\n- learner_aggregations\n- learning_item_aggregations\n- learner_assignments\n- learning_item_assignments\n- learning_records\n- other"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Supported Intent?"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1763145701482",
            "false": "1766193353866"
          },
          "code": "SUPPORTED_INTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1763334398001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763334398002_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINE_USER_INTENT.$output !== \"other\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Payload Templates"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762562531858"
          },
          "code": "SET_PAYLOAD_TEMPLATES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1763334832403",
          "id": "1763145701482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763145985314",
              "name": "payloadForData",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{\n  \"query\": \"\",\n  \"searchFields\": [\n    \"learningItemTitle\",\n    \"assignmentRecordNumber\",\n    \"learningItemNumber\",\n    \"DisplayName\",\n    \"Username\",\n    \"PersonNumber\",\n    \"WorkEmail\"\n  ],\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignedToId\", \"term\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"learningItemId\", \"term\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentRecordNumber\", \"term\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"learningItemNumber\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"assignedDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentDueDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"completedDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"expirationDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"learningFormat\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"learningItemTypev2\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentSubStatus\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentType\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"assignerDisplayName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"BusinessTitle\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"JobName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"DepartmentName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"PositionName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"LocationName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"BusinessUnitName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"LegalEmployerName\", \"terms\": [] },\n    { \"name\": \"GradeName\", \"terms\": [] },\n  ],\n  \"sort\": [],\n  \"_sortSupportedFields_learning_item_aggregations\": [\n    \"overdueLearning\",\n    \"enrollments\",\n    \"learningItemTitle\"\n  ],\n  \"_sortSupportedFields_learner_aggregations\": [\n    \"overdueLearning\",\n    \"enrollments\",\n    \"assignedToDisplayName\"\n  ],\n  \"_sortSupportedFields_learning_records\": [\n    \"learningItemTitle\",\n    \"learningItemNumber\",\n    \"learningItemTypev2\",\n    \"assignmentSubStatus\",\n    \"assignedDate\",\n    \"completedDate\",\n    \"assignmentDueDate\",\n    \"expirationDate\",\n    \"BusinessTitle\",\n    \"WorkerType\",\n    \"JobName\",\n    \"DepartmentName\",\n    \"PositionName\",\n    \"LocationName\",\n    \"BusinessUnitName\",\n    \"LegalEmployerName\",\n    \"GradeName\"\n  ],\n  \"_sortDirections\": [\n    \"asc\",\n    \"desc\"\n  ],\n  \"offset\": 0,\n  \"limit\": 100\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1763145971796",
              "name": "payloadForFacets",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{\n  \"query\": \"\",\n  \"searchFields\": [\n    \"learningItemTitle\",\n    \"assignmentRecordNumber\",\n    \"learningItemNumber\",\n    \"DisplayName\",\n    \"Username\",\n    \"PersonNumber\",\n    \"WorkEmail\"\n  ],\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"facetValueQuery\": \"\",\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignedDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentDueDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"completedDate\", \"value\": \"\" },\n    { \"name\": \"expirationDate\", \"value\": \"\" }\n  ],\n  \"facets\": [\n    \"learningItemTypev2\",\n    \"assignmentSubStatus\",\n    \"assignmentType\",\n    \"assignerDisplayName\",\n    \"BusinessTitle\",\n    \"WorkerType\",\n    \"JobName\",\n    \"JobCode\",\n    \"DepartmentName\",\n    \"PositionName\",\n    \"PositionCode\",\n    \"LocationCode\",\n    \"LocationName\",\n    \"BusinessUnitName\",\n    \"LegalEmployerName\",\n    \"GradeName\",\n    \"GradeCode\",\n    \"learningFormat\"\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Facet LOVs Payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764026748821"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_FACET_LOVS_PAYLOAD",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1763334894659",
          "id": "1762562531858",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762562531863_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou construct a facet-LOV request payload for learning record aggregations. Analyze the manager’s question and (optionally) recent context to produce a minimal, precise JSON payload to retrieve facet values relevant to the question. Include strict guardrails for enums and omit unsupported or empty values. Apply a facet-first strategy: prefer facets over query/searchFields for the same attribute, and prevent conflicts.\n\nHard guardrails (strict)\n- Output must be a single valid JSON object.\n- No markdown, no code fences, no comments, no trailing commas, no serialized-JSON strings.\n- No explanations or extra text before/after the JSON.\n- Do not add fields beyond those specified below.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</user_question>\n- Payload template (JSON):\n  <payload_template>{{$context.$variables.payloadForFacets}}</payload_template>\n- Chat history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$variables.chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- Data history (newest last; may be empty/null). Each record: { timestamp, userIntent, runData }:\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nAuthoritative whitelists (derived from the template)\n- allowed_facets = the exact strings in payload_template.facets.\n- allowed_search_fields = the exact strings in payload_template.searchFields.\n- identity_fields = [\"DisplayName\",\"Username\",\"PersonNumber\",\"WorkEmail\"] (never facets).\n\nBaseline scope filters (always-on, intent-aware)\n- Always include both filters with values chosen from these enums:\n  - reports ∈ { DIRECT_REPORTS, ALL_REPORTS }\n  - enrollments ∈ { CURRENT, PAST, ALL }\n- Selection rules (apply in order; fail-closed to defaults on ambiguity):\n  1) Explicit user wording → map directly to the enum.\n     - reports: DIRECT_REPORTS (“my team,” “my directs,” “my reports,” “direct reports”); ALL_REPORTS (“my org,” “entire org,” “all reports,” “everyone under me,” “whole chain”).\n     - enrollments: CURRENT (“current,” “active,” “assigned,” “overdue,” “due soon,” “in progress”); PAST (“completions,” “completed only,” “history”); ALL (“everything,” “both completed and current”).\n  2) If not explicit, inherit a clear setting from data_history by scanning newest→oldest and using the most recent record’s runData only when it contains a single, unambiguous, compatible setting; otherwise, inherit from chat_history (newest→oldest).\n  3) If still unclear, use defaults: reports = DIRECT_REPORTS; enrollments = CURRENT.\n- Guardrails: never omit these filters or leave them empty; emit only allowed enum values; widen scope only when clearly requested.\n\nFacet-first decision order (conflict-safe)\n1) Choose facets (subset of allowed_facets) relevant to the question/history.\n2) Allocate tokens:\n   - Tokens that target chosen facet attributes → facetValueQuery (only if exactly one facet).\n   - Tokens that target non-facet attributes → query/searchFields.\n3) Remove conflicts:\n   - If an attribute appears in facets, do not include that attribute in searchFields.\n   - Ensure query/searchFields never filter out values for attributes represented as facets.\n\nImportant constraint\n- learningItemTitle is NOT a facet. Never include it in facets or facetValueQuery. Route title keywords only to query/searchFields when appropriate.\n\nYour task\n- Start from payload_template and build a payload that:\n  - Hard-codes securityFilters.type = \"MANAGER\".\n  - Facets: include ONLY attributes clearly relevant to the question AND in allowed_facets. If none, set \"facets\": [].\n  - Filters: include the baseline scope filters and ONLY additional attributes/values confidently inferred (validated per rules below). Otherwise omit additional filters.\n  - Apply the facet-first token routing and conflict-removal rules.\n  - Query/searchFields: map an explicit search term only for attributes not represented as facets.\n  - Do not invent values. Omit any facet, filter, or field you cannot infer.\n\nHistory-aware token sourcing (secondary; fail-closed)\n- Prefer data_history (scan newest→oldest runData) over chat_history for resolving brief references and single clear tokens.\n- Candidate tokens (trim, deduplicate):\n  - Item: learningItemTitle substrings (query-only), learningItemNumber (OLC), assignmentRecordNumber.\n  - Learner: assignedToDisplayName substrings, Username, PersonNumber, WorkEmail.\n- Selection: prefer tokens explicitly referenced in user_question. If multiple candidates exist, pick a single most recent, clearly referenced token; if ambiguous, omit.\n\nFacetValueQuery (strict; single-facet gate)\n- Only include facetValueQuery if BOTH:\n  1) facets array length == 1, and\n  2) a clear substring token targets that single facet.\n- If facets.length > 1, do NOT include facetValueQuery (drop it).\n- The string must be non-empty and trimmed.\n- When facetValueQuery is present, remove that facet’s attribute from searchFields.\n- Never route learningItemTitle to facetValueQuery (it is query-only).\n\nQuery and searchFields mapping (non-facet attributes only; hard gate)\n- Include query ONLY if it is a non-empty, trimmed string.\n- Include searchFields ONLY if query is present and non-empty and searchFields is a non-empty subset of allowed_search_fields; otherwise omit BOTH.\n- Item-related tokens → [\"learningItemTitle\",\"learningItemNumber\",\"assignmentRecordNumber\"] ∩ allowed_search_fields, minus any attributes present in facets.\n- Learner-related tokens → subset of identity_fields ∩ allowed_search_fields.\n- If query is omitted, also omit searchFields.\n\nFilters (strict whitelist; inference + validation)\n- Only the following additional filters are allowed (per template). Include them only when explicit/safely deducible and non-empty:\n  - assignedDate (value), assignmentDueDate (value), completedDate (value), expirationDate (value), createdBy (value).\n  - reports (value), enrollments (value) [baseline; see above].\n- IDs/codes (e.g., assignedToId, learningItemId, learningItemNumber) are not part of the facet-LOV filter whitelist; do not emit them here.\n\nDate filter validation and normalization (STRICT; facet payload)\n- Allowed tokens by field:\n  - assignedDate: { LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_03_MONTHS, LAST_12_MONTHS, YEAR_TO_DATE, ALL_TIME }\n  - completedDate: { LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_03_MONTHS, LAST_12_MONTHS, YEAR_TO_DATE, ALL_TIME }\n  - assignmentDueDate: { NEXT_30_DAYS, NEXT_12_MONTHS, LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_12_MONTHS, ALL_TIME }\n  - expirationDate: { NEXT_30_DAYS, NEXT_12_MONTHS, LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_12_MONTHS, ALL_TIME }\n  - createdBy (enum, not a date): { ME, ALL }\n- Normalize common user phrases only to the correct field. If the normalized value is not in the allowed set, omit the filter.\n\nFinal sanitation (must apply before returning JSON)\n- If query is missing, null, \"\", or only whitespace OR searchFields is missing or []:\n  - Remove both query and searchFields from the payload.\n- If facetValueQuery is missing, null, \"\", or only whitespace OR facets.length !== 1:\n  - Remove facetValueQuery from the payload.\n- Remove any property whose value is null/undefined/\"\" or an empty array/object, except the required baseline scope filters.\n- Ensure the result is valid JSON (no dangling commas, no empty keys).\n\nFinal validation (fail-closed)\n- Ensure at least one of: non-empty query OR non-empty filters (baseline scope filters satisfy this if no query).\n- facets ⊆ allowed_facets (and never include learningItemTitle).\n- searchFields ⊆ allowed_search_fields and exclude any attribute present in facets.\n\nOutput format (strict)\n- Return ONLY one well-formed JSON object.\n- Must include:\n  - securityFilters with type \"MANAGER\"\n  - filters with baseline scope entries (reports, enrollments) and any validated date filters\n  - facets (may be [])\n- Conditional:\n  - additional filters only if present and valid\n  - facetValueQuery only when the strict conditions are met\n  - query/searchFields only when query is present, non-empty, and not in conflict with facets\n\nExamples (illustrative only; follow rules above; do not emit these literally)\nExample: Org-wide scope from wording “my whole organization”\nUser: Current learning items for my whole organization.\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"ALL_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" }\n  ],\n  \"facets\": []\n}\nExample: Directs scope\nUser: Show current learning items for my directs.\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" }\n  ],\n  \"facets\": [\"learningItemTypev2\"]\n}\nExample 3: Date mapping with strict enums (single date field; no facetValueQuery)\nUser: Due next month for my directs\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignmentDueDate\", \"value\": \"NEXT_30_DAYS\" }\n  ],\n  \"facets\": [\"assignmentType\"]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Data Payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766194141772"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_DATA_PAYLOAD",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1763334894659",
          "id": "1763146938364",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763146938365_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou build the final request payload for the main data fetch. Use the facet LOVs context, the manager’s question, and recent context to produce concrete, minimal filters. Only include fields that are explicitly requested or safely inferred, and never include empty or unsupported filter values. Convert facet selections into filters using the LOV value token only (never displayValue). The final data payload must not contain facets; instead, its filters combine: (a) concrete, valid filters from the facet-LOV payload, (b) facet-derived filters converted from facet LOV results, and (c) intent-specific filters added by this step when applicable (assignedToId for learner_assignments; learningItemId for learning_item_assignments).\n\nHard guardrails (strict)\n- Output must be a single valid JSON object.\n- No markdown, no code fences, no comments, no trailing commas, no serialized-JSON strings.\n- Do not include explanations or extra text before/after the JSON.\n- Do not add fields not specified below.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$variables.userQuery}}</user_question>\n- Current routing intent (one of: learning_item_aggregations, learner_aggregations, learning_records, learner_assignments, learning_item_assignments):\n  <current_intent>{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINE_USER_INTENT.$output}}</current_intent>\n- Base payload template (JSON):\n  <base_payload_template>{{$context.$variables.payloadForData}}</base_payload_template>\n- Facet LOVs payload you previously created (may include initial filters and query/searchFields):\n  <facet_lovs_payload>{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_FACET_LOVS_PAYLOAD.$output}}</facet_lovs_payload>\n- Facet LOVs results (JSON with facets and values):\n  <facet_lovs_results>{{$context.$nodes.GET_FACET_LOVS.$output}}</facet_lovs_results>\n- Facets mapped flag (boolean):\n  <facets_mapped>{{$context.$nodes.FACETS_MAPPED.$output.result}}</facets_mapped>\n- Chat history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- Data history (newest last; may be empty/null). Each record: { timestamp, userIntent, runData }:\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nBaseline scope filters (always-on, intent-aware)\n- Always include both filters with values chosen from these enums:\n  - reports ∈ { DIRECT_REPORTS, ALL_REPORTS }\n  - enrollments ∈ { CURRENT, PAST, ALL }\n- Selection rules (apply in order; fail-closed to defaults on ambiguity):\n  1) Explicit user wording → map directly to the enum.\n     - reports: DIRECT_REPORTS (“my team,” “my directs,” “my reports,” “direct reports”); ALL_REPORTS (“my org,” “entire org,” “all reports,” “everyone under me,” “whole chain”).\n     - enrollments: CURRENT (“current,” “active,” “assigned,” “overdue,” “due soon,” “in progress”); PAST (“completions,” “completed only,” “history”); ALL (“everything,” “both completed and current”).\n  2) If not explicit, inherit a clear setting from data_history (scan newest→oldest records and use the most recent record’s runData only if it contains an unambiguous, compatible setting); otherwise from chat_history (newest→oldest).\n  3) If still unclear, use defaults: reports = DIRECT_REPORTS; enrollments = CURRENT.\n- Guardrails: never omit these filters or leave them empty; emit only allowed enum values; widen scope only when clearly requested.\n\nObjective\n- Start from base_payload_template.\n- Build a new filters array that is the union of:\n  1) Concrete, valid filters from facet_lovs_payload.filters (plus the baseline scope filters), and\n  2) Facet-derived filters converted from facet_lovs_results (only if facets_mapped = true), and\n  3) Intent-specific filters added by this step when applicable (assignedToId for learner_assignments; learningItemId for learning_item_assignments).\n- Do not include facets or facetValueQuery in the data payload.\n\nQuery/searchFields (hard gate, aggregation-aware)\n- Only include query if it is a non-empty, trimmed string; only include searchFields if query is present and non-empty and searchFields is a non-empty subset of the template’s allowed search fields.\n- Copy query/searchFields from facet_lovs_payload only when BOTH are present and non-empty; otherwise omit both.\n- Aggregation intents (learning_item_aggregations, learner_aggregations): do not invent a query; omit query/searchFields unless the user provided a clear keyword/code (e.g., title substring, OLC code). Prefer filters and sort for “top/most/fewest” requests.\n- Conflict-avoidance with filters:\n  - If a filter exists for an attribute, do NOT include that attribute in searchFields and do NOT route query to it.\n  - If this removal empties searchFields, omit query and searchFields entirely.\n- History-aware enrichment (secondary; fail-closed): You may set/adjust query only if a single clear token appears in data_history (preferred; scan newest→oldest runData) or chat_history and targets attributes not represented as filters and present in the allowed searchFields.\n\nFacet-derived filters (history-aware; strict to LOVs; value-only)\n- Only if facets_mapped = true:\n  - For each facet present in facet_lovs_results and relevant to the user question/recent context:\n    - Convert selected values to a filter:\n      { \"name\": \"<FacetName>\", \"terms\": [\"<value1>\", \"<value2>\", ...] }\n    - Always emit the LOV value token (never displayValue).\n    - Match context to LOV entries case-insensitively, but emit the exact value strings from facet_lovs_results.\n    - If multiple values match or mapping is ambiguous, skip that facet.\n  - Do not create filters for identity fields (DisplayName, Username, PersonNumber, WorkEmail).\n\nNon-facet filters\n- Start from facet_lovs_payload.filters and preserve ONLY those that are concrete and valid; refine only if clearly supported by the user question or recent context.\n- IDs must be digits-only strings (assignedToId, learningItemId, managerId).\n- assignmentRecordNumber must be an explicit record number (e.g., OLC123456).\n- learningItemNumber must be an explicit OLC-like code.\n\nLearner-specific targeting (assignedToId) — applies only when current_intent == \"learner_assignments\"\n- Processing order (learner_assignments):\n  1) Copy query/searchFields from facet_lovs_payload if BOTH are non-empty and allowed.\n  2) Attempt assignedToId resolution and injection (see below).\n  3) Apply compatibility pruning ONLY if assignedToId is injected; otherwise keep identity queries.\n- Resolution order (fail-closed):\n  1) From user_question (explicit numeric only and clearly labeled, e.g., “assignedToId 300100…” or “learner id 300100…”).\n  2) From data_history (scan newest→oldest; use an exact name→ID mapping in runData with an unambiguous single match; never name-as-ID).\n  3) From chat_history (same mapping; newest→oldest; unambiguous single match).\n- Guardrails:\n  - Digits-only; trimmed; not \"0\".\n  - Never use names/emails/usernames in the ID field.\n- Payload update:\n  - Ensure filters exists; remove any existing { \"name\":\"assignedToId\", … }.\n  - Insert exactly one: { \"name\":\"assignedToId\", \"term\":\"<ID>\" }.\n- Query/searchFields compatibility with assignedToId (keep by default; prune only on conflict):\n  - identity_fields = [\"DisplayName\",\"Username\",\"PersonNumber\",\"WorkEmail\"]\n  - item_query_fields = [\"learningItemTitle\",\"learningItemNumber\",\"assignmentRecordNumber\"]\n  - If assignedToId is injected:\n    - Keep query/searchFields if searchFields ⊆ item_query_fields and query is non-empty.\n    - Remove BOTH query and searchFields if searchFields contains any identity_fields (identity queries are redundant/conflicting once assignedToId is present), or if either is empty/whitespace.\n  - If assignedToId is NOT injected:\n    - Keep non-empty identity queries (DisplayName/Username/PersonNumber/WorkEmail) that are allowed by the template.\n\nItem-specific targeting (learningItemId) — applies only when current_intent == \"learning_item_assignments\"\n- Processing order (learning_item_assignments):\n  1) Copy query/searchFields from facet_lovs_payload if BOTH are non-empty and allowed.\n  2) Attempt learningItemId resolution and injection (see below).\n  3) Apply compatibility pruning ONLY if learningItemId is injected; otherwise keep item/identity queries.\n- Resolution order (fail-closed):\n  1) From user_question (explicit numeric only and clearly labeled, e.g., “learningItemId 300100…” or “item id 300100…”).\n  2) From data_history (scan newest→oldest; use an exact title→ID mapping in runData with an unambiguous single match; never title-as-ID).\n  3) From chat_history (same mapping; newest→oldest; unambiguous single match).\n- Guardrails:\n  - Digits-only; trimmed; not \"0\".\n  - Never use titles, OLC codes, emails, or any non-numeric token in the ID field.\n- Payload update:\n  - Ensure filters exists; remove any existing { \"name\":\"learningItemId\", … }.\n  - Insert exactly one: { \"name\":\"learningItemId\", \"term\":\"<ID>\" }.\n- Query/searchFields compatibility with learningItemId (keep by default; prune only on conflict):\n  - item_query_fields = [\"learningItemTitle\",\"learningItemNumber\",\"assignmentRecordNumber\"]\n  - identity_fields = [\"DisplayName\",\"Username\",\"PersonNumber\",\"WorkEmail\"]\n  - If learningItemId is injected:\n    - Keep identity-only queries (DisplayName/Username/PersonNumber/WorkEmail) when non-empty and allowed (they are compatible with a single item).\n    - Remove BOTH query and searchFields if searchFields includes any item_query_fields that do not clearly refer to the same item as the resolved learningItemId, or if either is empty/whitespace.\n    - If searchFields mixes item_query_fields with identity_fields, remove the conflicting item_query_fields and keep identity_fields if any remain; if none remain, remove BOTH.\n  - If learningItemId is NOT injected:\n    - Keep non-empty item queries (learningItemTitle/learningItemNumber/assignmentRecordNumber) and identity queries that are allowed by the template.\n\nDate filter validation and normalization (STRICT)\n- Allowed tokens by field:\n  - assignedDate: { LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_03_MONTHS, LAST_12_MONTHS, YEAR_TO_DATE, ALL_TIME }\n  - completedDate: { LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_03_MONTHS, LAST_12_MONTHS, YEAR_TO_DATE, ALL_TIME }\n  - assignmentDueDate: { NEXT_30_DAYS, NEXT_12_MONTHS, LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_12_MONTHS, ALL_TIME }\n  - expirationDate: { NEXT_30_DAYS, NEXT_12_MONTHS, LAST_30_DAYS, LAST_12_MONTHS, ALL_TIME }\n  - createdBy (enum, not a date): { ME, ALL }\n- Normalize common user phrases only to the correct field. If the normalized value is not in the allowed set, omit the filter.\n- learningItemCreationDate (range): include only if both from/to are valid YYYY-MM-DD.\n\nSorting (intent-specific; no defaults)\n- Never include a default sort. Emit sort only when explicitly requested by the user or safely inferred from clear phrases. Validate sort names against the appropriate supported list in base_payload_template:\n  - For learning_item_aggregations: validate against _sortSupportedFields_learning_item_aggregations.\n    - Mappings: “most overdue/overdue first” → overdueLearning desc; “least overdue” → overdueLearning asc; “most/fewest enrollments” → enrollments desc/asc; “alphabetical” → learningItemTitle asc.\n  - For learner_aggregations: validate against _sortSupportedFields_learner_aggregations.\n    - Mappings: “most/least overdue” → overdueLearning desc/asc; “most assigned” → enrollments desc; “alphabetical by name” → assignedToDisplayName asc.\n  - For learning_records, learner_assignments, learning_item_assignments: validate against _sortSupportedFields_learning_records.\n    - Mappings: “soonest due/next due first” → assignmentDueDate asc; “latest due dates” → assignmentDueDate desc; “most recent assignments” → assignedDate desc; “most recent completions” → completedDate desc; “alphabetical by name” → DisplayName asc.\n- If a requested/inferred sort name is not present in the corresponding list, omit sort.\n- Emit a single sort array; if multiple criteria are explicitly requested, preserve their order and validate each against the list for the current intent.\n\nConcrete filter rules (must pass ALL checks)\n- Each filter must have a non-empty name and one of:\n  - value (non-empty, allowed enum if applicable), OR\n  - term (non-empty), OR\n  - terms (array with at least one non-empty string), OR\n  - range with valid from/to (date-only where supported).\n- Reject empty/invalid filters and remove duplicates (keep last valid).\n\nField exclusions and minimalism\n- Do not include facets or facetValueQuery in the data payload.\n- Include query and searchFields only when both are non-empty and not in conflict with filters; otherwise omit both.\n- Always include securityFilters with type \"MANAGER\", and offset and limit from base_payload_template.\n\nFinal sanitation (must apply before returning JSON)\n- If query is missing, null, \"\", or only whitespace OR searchFields is missing or []: remove BOTH.\n- For learner_assignments when assignedToId was applied:\n  - Ensure exactly one assignedToId filter exists.\n  - Ensure no empty/invalid query/searchFields remain after compatibility pruning; remove identity-based query/searchFields if present.\n- For learning_item_assignments when learningItemId was applied:\n  - Ensure exactly one learningItemId filter exists.\n  - Ensure no empty/invalid query/searchFields remain after compatibility pruning; remove conflicting item-field queries if present.\n- Remove any property whose value is null/undefined/\"\" or an empty array/object, except the required baseline scope filters.\n- Ensure the result is valid JSON (no dangling commas, no empty keys).\n\nEdge cases\n- If the user question is too vague to determine any filters beyond security and pagination, return payload with just securityFilters, offset, limit; no additional filters and no query/searchFields; no sort.\n- If facets_mapped is true but no resolvable facet values match the question or recent context, do not add any facet-derived filters.\n\nOutput requirements (strict)\n- Return ONLY one well-formed JSON object representing the final request payload.\n- Must include:\n  - securityFilters with type \"MANAGER\"\n  - offset and limit from the template\n  - baseline scope filters (reports, enrollments)\n- Must NOT include:\n  - facets\n  - facetValueQuery\n  - markdown code fences, comments, trailing commas\n- Conditional presence:\n  - filters: include only if at least one concrete filter remains (baseline scope always ensures non-empty).\n  - query/searchFields: include only when both are non-empty and not conflicting with filters.\n  - sort: include only when explicitly requested or safely inferred (and supported by the corresponding _sortSupportedFields_* list).\n\nExamples (illustrative only; follow rules above; do not emit these literally)\nExample 1 — learner_assignments: keep identity query when no assignedToId is injected\nIntent: learner_assignments\nUser: Show Ravi’s courses\nOutput:\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"offset\": 0,\n  \"limit\": 100,\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" }\n  ],\n  \"query\": \"Ravi\",\n  \"searchFields\": [\"DisplayName\"]\n}\nExample 2 — learner_assignments: inject assignedToId, then prune identity query\nIntent: learner_assignments\nUser: Show Ravi’s assignments\nOutput:\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": { \"type\": \"MANAGER\" },\n  \"offset\": 0,\n  \"limit\": 100,\n  \"filters\": [\n    { \"name\": \"reports\", \"value\": \"DIRECT_REPORTS\" },\n    { \"name\": \"enrollments\", \"value\": \"CURRENT\" },\n    { \"name\": \"assignedToId\", \"term\": \"300100546156849\" }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
